  "scope": "Exact-source reverse-engineering of story placement selection for the player tent, first bridge, and three settler plots; StructurePresetA00 site-list loading; native transform/consumer join search. No Godot, build, or game execution.",
  "finding": "EventFlow passes explicit StructureType and StructureBuildPosType values to generic preview/build actions. FieldMainFieldParam row UniqueID 0 selects StructurePresetA00, which contains six ordered mSiteList s32 cell pairs. A later native follow-up confirms that the registered BuildStructure candidate selects an available six-list index, writes it under the actor AI blackboard key BuildingSiteIndex, parses the cell pair, and passes it to actor-context handling. No source assigns a specific story building to an index or establishes the runtime preset instance, world transform, footprint, model, save record, or collider.",
  "labels": {
    "EF": "EventFlow graph evidence only; runtime handler behavior is not proven.",
    "TBL": "BCSV row/column evidence; identifiers are table-local absent an explicit join.",
    "STRUCT": "Parsed BYML structure; cell values do not establish world transforms or semantic site roles.",
    "PSEUDO": "Static analysis/decompiler output, not native execution.",
    "OPEN": "Required source, consumer, transform, instance, model, or collider join not established.",
    "CAT": "Catalog candidate only; not used to prove placement, model, or collider consumers here."
  },
